;
; VAG-COM Labelfile
;
; Audi A6 (4F)
;
; Component: J386 - Driver's Door Electronics (#42)
;
; P/N: 4F0-910-793-???
;
; includes measuring blocks, coding and selective output test
;
; This file is part of a redirection package,
; make sure you have all of the following files.
;
; 4F-42.LBL
; 4F0-910-793-42.LBL
;
; created on 16/Oct/2005 by Sebastian Stange (sebastian@ross-tech.com)
;
; last modification: 19/Nov/2005
;
; requires VAG-COM 505.1 or newer
;
;
;---------------------------------------------------
;
; coding information
;
;---------------------------------------------------
;
;
C00,Driver's Door Electronics (J386) Coding
C01,+0000001 - Fuel Tank Lid Unlock Button (PR-A8U)
C02,+0000002 - Interior Door Handle Illumination (Standard)
C03,+0000004 - Insulated Glass installed (PR-4KR/4KV)
C04,+0000008 - Door Warning Lights (Standard)
C05,+0000016 - Right Hand Steering (PR-L0R)
C06,+0000032 - Lighting Package (Interior Lighting - PR-QQ1)
C07,+0000064 - Lighting Package (Exterior Lighting - PR-QQ1)
C08,+0000128 - Outside Mirror Adjustment (Memory - PR-6XF/6XL)
C09,+0000256 - Without Mirror Heating
C10,+0000512 - Interior Lock Switch
C11,+0001024 - Avant (Wagon)
C12,+0002048 - Electrical Child Safety Lock (PR-4H5)
C13,+0004096 - Opening Assistance
C14,+0008192 - Closing Assistance (PR-GZ2)
C15,+0016384 - Keyless-Entry (PR-4F2/4K5/4K7)
C16,+0032768 - Without Safe Function (PR-A8U)
C17,+0065536 - Window Regulator Comfort Function
C18,+0131072 - Handicapped Vehicle
C19,+0262144 - Special Protection Vehicle
;
;
;---------------------------------------------------
;
; selective output test information
;
;---------------------------------------------------
;
;
T1482,Motors for Central Locking
T2111,Motor for Window Regulator
T2117,Motor for Mirror Folding
T2188,Lighting/Illumination
T2189,Mirror Function Test
;
;
;---------------------------------------------------
;
; measuring block information
;
;---------------------------------------------------
;
;
001,1,Door Status,,Display Range: 0 = inactive / 1 = active\n\nxxxxxxx? = Key Switch open\nxxxxxx?x = Key Switch closed\nxxxxx?xx = Central Locking (CL) Interior Switch locking\nxxxx?xxx = Central Locking (CL) Interior Switch unlocking\nxxx?xxxx = Lock Feedback "locked"\nxx?xxxxx = Lock Feedback "safed" (not USA)\nx?xxxxxx = Door Contact Switch\n?xxxxxxx = Catch (for Closing Assistance)
001,2,Button Status,,Display Range: 0 = inactive / 1 = active\n\nxxxxxxx? = Interior Door Handle Button\nxxxxxx?x = External Door Handle Button\nxxxxx?xx = Rear Lid Remote Control Lock Button\nxxxx?xxx = Fuel Tank Lid Unlock Button\nxxx?xxxx = Child Safety Button (Left)\nxx?xxxxx = Child Safety Button (Right)\nx?xxxxxx = Interior Monitoring Button (not USA)\n?xxxxxxx = Alarm System OFF Button
001,3,Voltages and,Databus Status,Display Range: 0 = inactive / 1 = active\n\n0000xxx? = Terminal 30 (Window Regulator)\n0000xx?x = Terminal 30 (Central Locking)\n0000x?xx = Terminal 15\n0000?xxx = CAN-Comfort in Single-Wire Mode
001,4,Voltage Supply
;
002,0,Window Regulator Buttons (Local)
002,1,WR-Button (E40),Drivers Door,Display Range: Auto Open/Auto Close/Manual Open/Manual Close/Not Oper.
002,2,WR-Button (E81),Passenger Door,Display Range: Auto Open/Auto Close/Manual Open/Manual Close/Not Oper.
002,3,WR-Button (E53),Rear Left Door,Display Range: Auto Open/Auto Close/Manual Open/Manual Close/Not Oper.
002,4,WR-Button (E55),Rear Right Door,Display Range: Auto Open/Auto Close/Manual Open/Manual Close/Not Oper.
;
003,1,Window Regulator,Position,Display Range: 0.0...100.0 %
003,2,Window Regulator,Motor Temperature,Display Range: -50.0...+200.0 °C
003,3,Window Regulator,Status,Display Range: 0 = inactive / 1 = active\n\nxxx? = Window Regulators present\nxx?x = Thermal Protection\nx?xx = Standardized\n?xxx = Insulated Glass
003,4,Window Regulator,Movement,Display Range: Still/Open/Closed
;
004,1,Mirror,Adjustment Switch,Display Range: Pos X+/Pos X-/Pos Y+/Pos Y-/Not Oper./Not Installed
004,2,Mirror,Selector Switch,Display Range: Left/Right/Fold In/Not Installed/Implausible
;
005,1,Vehicle Speed,,Display Range: 0.0...255.0 km/h
005,2,Ambient,Temperature,Display Range: -50.0...+200.0 °C
005,3,Mirror Heating,(calculated),Display Range: 0.0...100.0 %
005,4,Mirror Heating,Status,Display Rannge: Heater Off/Heater On
;
006,1,Memory Buttons,,Display Range: 0 = inactive / 1 = active\n\nxxxxx? = Memory Button\nxxxx?x = Emergency-Off Button\nxxx?xx = Position Button 1\nxx?xxx = Position Button 2\nx?xxxx = Position Button 3\n?xxxxx = Position Button 4
006,2,Mirror Position X,(Potentiometer),Display Range: 0.0...5.0 V
006,3,Mirror Position Y,(Potentiometer),Display Range: 0.0...5.0 V
006,4,Miscellaneous,,00000001 = Kessy Lock Button active
;
007,1,Closing,Assistance,Display Range: Not Installed
007,2,Opening,Assistance,Display Range: Not Installed
007,3,Child Safety,Lock Button,Display Range: Operated/Not Oper./Not Installed
007,4,Window Regulator,Current Consumpt.
;
